# HomeBase environment variables
#
# You normally don't fill this in by hand. The project is linked to Vercel
# (`vercel link`) and most of these are provisioned by Vercel integrations, so:
#
#     vercel env pull .env.local
#
# fetches real values for everything below. This file documents what each one
# is for and which are required.

# --- Database (Neon, via Vercel Marketplace) -------------------------------
# DATABASE_URL           Pooled connection — used for the app's runtime queries.
# DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED  Direct/non-pooled connection — used ONLY by drizzle-kit
#                        migrations. The pooled connection (PgBouncer, transaction
#                        mode) doesn't support the session-level operations
#                        migrations need, so don't point drizzle.config.ts at it.

# --- Attachments (Vercel Blob) ---------------------------------------------
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN  Blob store "homebase". Backs photo/receipt/manual/document
#                        uploads across bills, readings, maintenance, inventory,
#                        repairs and the document vault.

# --- AI extraction (Google Gemini, free tier) ------------------------------
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY
#                        Powers "Scan with AI" on bills and meter readings.
#                        Optional: without it those buttons fail gracefully and
#                        the manual forms still work exactly as normal.

# --- Web push reminders -----------------------------------------------------
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY
#                        VAPID public key. Safe to expose — it's sent to the
#                        browser to create a push subscription.
# VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY      VAPID private key. SECRET. Signs outgoing push messages.
# VAPID_SUBJECT          Contact URI for the push service, e.g. mailto:you@example.com
# CRON_SECRET            Random string (32+ chars). Vercel sends it as
#                        `Authorization: Bearer <value>` when invoking cron jobs;
#                        /api/cron/notify rejects anything else with a 401.
#
# To regenerate the VAPID pair from scratch (invalidates existing subscriptions,
# so every device must re-enable reminders afterwards):
#
#     node -e "console.log(require('web-push').generateVAPIDKeys())"
